	(text_box "The buck-boost is a voltage converter that takes in the highly variable battery voltage (6.4-8.4V) and gives out a relatively stable output. However, it is noisy as it is a switching regulator and we desire low noise for our application, so we put in cascade an LDO. The resistors and capacitance are chosen according to the IC's datasheet."
